@nsobid-7E1DF8E08D60544BBDCA1E333C153C97

# Xenoblade Chronicles: Definitive Edition 2.0.0 - Disable anti-aliasing

@flag print_values
@flag offset_shift 0x100

// Disables the game's anti-aliasing: FXAA in the final composite and the
// temporal AA (tmaa).
//
// Both are switches in the post-effect parameter file the renderer parses
// (sub_629BB0): "AntiAliasing" and "tmaa", each "on" or "off". sub_6B2510
// copies them into the frame's render state (+0xFC and +0x111), sub_6B1AF0
// resets the state with AntiAliasing on, and sub_697B30 turns tmaa on for the
// scenes it sets up. When either is on, the frame ends in the AA composite
// (FXAA) or the temporal resolve, and tmaa also drives the temporal history and
// jitter users.
//
// Every write of the two switches now stores off. The frame then takes the
// renderer's own no-AA final composite, the path the parameter file selects
// when both are set to off, so FXAA, the temporal resolve and its jitter all
// stop.

@enabled
00698198 1F450439   // STRB WZR,[X8,#0x111]: tmaa stays off (was STRB W23 = on)
006B1CA8 1FF00339   // STRB WZR,[X0,#0xFC]: reset leaves AntiAliasing off (was STRB W11 = on)
006B2588 7FF20339   // STRB WZR,[X19,#0xFC]: AntiAliasing off for render mode 1, which forces it on (was STRB W20)
006B2620 7F460439   // STRB WZR,[X19,#0x111]: tmaa off (was STRB W8 = parameter file value)
006B2628 7FF20339   // STRB WZR,[X19,#0xFC]: AntiAliasing off (was STRB W8 = parameter file value)
@stop

// Offsets reverse-engineered against Xenoblade Chronicles: Definitive Edition
// 2.0.0 (Monolith engine, NVN). The retail build is symbol-stripped; every site
// was located by structure and byte-verified against the IDB before being
// written.
//
// https://github.com/RAMDRAGONS/switch-patches
